<title>CHILE: Chilean worker dies in copper mine.</title>
<headline>Chilean worker dies in copper mine.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Chilean worker in the El Teniente copper mine of the state-owned National Copper Corporation (CODELCO) died in a work accident, the company said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The miner, Gustavo Zamora, 49, &quot;suffered an accident that took away his life,&quot; CODELCO said.</p>
<p>It added that the circumstances surrounding the Saturday night accident will be investigated.</p>
<p>Zamora fell 60 feet (20 meters) into one of the mine's tunnels, the company said.</p>
